# Prisma stores a checksum of each applied migration.sql and re-verifies it
# on every migrate dev/deploy. CRLF conversion changes the bytes and breaks
# that check. Keep SQL as LF on every platform.
*.sql text eol=lf


# Added 15 August 2026. See Ultra 36 trap #192.
#
# This repo accumulated mixed CRLF and LF files, which broke multi-line
# installer anchors four times in one session: an anchor written with LF
# silently misses a CRLF file even though every line is present. The rule
# above pinned .sql only, for Prisma's checksum - nothing covered source.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT RENORMALIZED. `git add --renormalize .` would rewrite
# every file in the repository and bury the next real change in noise.
# Files normalize as they are touched.

* text=auto

*.ts     text eol=lf
*.tsx    text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Windows-native, and this session found the PowerShell parser fussy enough
# not to gamble on it.
*.ps1    text eol=crlf